  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Green Local Currency Intermediated Lending in Tunisia via TCX Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The Green Local Currency Intermediated Lending in Tunisia via TCX Fund is designed to enable IFIs to improve the ability of Tunisian banks (&#xBF;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Banks&lt;/strong&gt;&#xBF; or &#xBF;&lt;strong&gt;PBs&lt;/strong&gt;&#xBF;) to finance SMEs engaged in the green transition and to help them resume growth in the post-crisis period.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;specific objectives&lt;/strong&gt; of the Programme are as follows:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;i.to enable a resumption of medium- and long-term IFI lending to PBs at a viable cost for on-lending to the local economy;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;ii.to support medium local-currency lending to businesses, including SMEs;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;iii.to support a sustainable and green post-pandemic economic recovery in the country ;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;iv.to strengthen the financial system through support for critical foreign-exchange hedging activities;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;v.to promote more equitable access to climate finance for women-led SMEs in the region via mainstreaming gender considerations into project design and delivery.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Action aims to address the absence of sustainable hedging instruments in the country preventing Tunisian banks to access international medium-term financing. Although the relevance of all these objectives was demonstrated prior to the onset of the COVID-19 pandemic, higher importance is attached to them in the context of the economic crisis that has followed the pandemic and the current war in Ukraine. The country is cash-strapped and needs more financing for its budget. Therefore, it is critical to provide urgent support to offset and mitigate the impact of the war in Ukraine (i.e. energy and food security), while focusing on medium and long term support to ensure macroeconomic stability and growth, improved business climate, and job creation.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
